"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[21102],{621102:e=>{e.exports="# Workday RAAS\n\n## Guidelines\n\n> **IMPORTANT** — You help the user **set up Workday RAAS ingestion in Databricks**. **Do not write data to Workday or modify the customer's Workday tenant** (no creates, updates, deletes, or configuration changes to business data or Workday setup). **Read-only** diagnostics are **appropriate**—including OAuth/basic checks to validate credentials, report URL validation, and **fetching samples or schema to confirm the report and fields are accessible**. Token calls in this skill exist solely to obtain read access for those checks, not to change Workday state beyond normal token refresh side effects.\n\n## Setting Up Workday RAAS\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- An **Integration System User (ISU)** with the appropriate Security Group granted access to each report being ingested\n- Either **OAuth API Client** credentials (client ID + client secret + refresh token) or **Basic Auth** (ISU username + password)\n\n### Report URL Format\n\nReport URLs must follow: `https://{host}/ccx/service/customreport2/{tenant}/{ISU_user}/{report_name}`\n\n- `{host}` — Workday host (e.g. `impl.workday.com`)\n- `{tenant}` — Workday tenant name\n- `{ISU_user}` — Integration System User username (must match the ISU that owns the report access)\n- `{report_name}` — exact name of the custom report\n\nThe ISU username in the URL must match the ISU that has been granted report access — a mismatch here causes 404 errors that look like the report doesn't exist.\n\n## Diagnosing Workday RAAS Connection\n\n### Diagnostic Flow\n\n#### Step 1: Get Report URLs\n\nCheck the agent context or available tools for the pipeline spec. The report URL is often already available — look for it before asking the user. Each configured report has a full Workday custom report URL (e.g. `https://{host}/ccx/service/customreport2/{tenant}/{user}/{report}`). These are the `reportUrl` values to pass to the diagnostic tools below.\n\n#### Step 2: Check Report Access\n\n1. Call `workday_fetchReport` with a `reportUrl` from Step 1.\n   - **Success with data** → report is accessible and returning rows.\n   - **Success with 0 rows** → report may be empty or filters exclude all data.\n   - **401** → credentials are invalid or expired. For OAuth: refresh token may need regenerating in Workday. For Basic: ISU username/password is wrong.\n   - **404 (REPORT_NOT_FOUND)** → report name is wrong, renamed, or ISU user in URL doesn't match.\n   - **500 with \"do not have access\"** → ISU lacks Security Group permissions for this report. Grant the ISU's Security Group access to the report's data source in Workday.\n   - **500 with \"do not have access to one or more fields\"** → ISU can access the report but lacks permissions for fields used in filters. Grant field-level access or remove restricted fields.\n   - **500 with \"does not have the required privileges\"** → OAuth API Client lacks required scopes. Add the relevant Functional Area scope in Workday, then generate a new refresh token.\n   - **Non-JSON response** → report didn't return JSON. The tool always requests `format=json`.\n\n#### Step 3: Check Schema\n\n1. Call `workday_fetchReportSchema` with a `reportUrl` from Step 1 to get the XSD schema.\n2. Parse field names and types from the XSD response.\n\n#### Step 4: Suggest Fix\n\nBased on results, tell the user what works, what doesn't, and what to fix (credentials, report URL, OAuth scopes, ISU permissions, or basic auth username/password).\n\n## Source Reference\n\n### Reports\n\nWorkday RAAS (Report-as-a-Service) exposes **Custom Reports** as REST endpoints returning XML or JSON. Each report is authored in Workday and can include calculated fields, filters, and joins across Workday business objects.\n\n- Report field names match Workday's internal field aliases, not the display labels shown in the Workday UI\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- Report not RAAS-enabled: the report must be **Advanced, Matrix, or Composite type** with **\"Enable As Web Service\"** checked in the Workday report definition — simple reports cannot be exposed as web services, and standard/delivered reports typically need to be copied as a custom report first before this option is available\n- Response times exceeding 30 minutes indicate timeout risk — check `elapsed_seconds` in tool response\n- Reports with >500K records are high risk for performance issues\n"}}]);
